course: dictionary
lesson: 2948
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and drill is one of them. Context tells you which meaning is right. «In an earthquake drill you drop, cover under a desk and hold on.» Here a drill is a practice, something you do again and again so you know what to do in danger.
explain: «Real woodpeckers drill holes to nest and to find insects.» Here drill means to make a hole. Ask yourself: what would fit? Holes fit the tool meaning, not the practice meaning. Try the meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
explain: Drill can also be a doing word, a verb. At the dentist, a drill cleans out a bad part of a tooth. Look for clues such as holes, practice, or safety to choose the right meaning.
fact: A drill can be a tool or machine for making holes in wood, metal, stone or teeth.
fact: A drill can be a practice of what to do in an emergency, such as a fire drill.
fact: A drill can be repeated practice to learn something well, such as a times-table drill.
fact: As a verb, «drill» means to make a hole with a drill, or to train by repeating.
fact: The phrase «the drill» means the usual way of doing something.
exercise: «In an earthquake drill you drop, cover under a desk and hold on.» What does drill mean here? | A sharp kind of pencil | A tool for making holes | *A practice of what to do in an emergency | A machine at the dentist
exercise: «Real woodpeckers drill holes to nest and to find insects.» What does drill mean here? | To practise a safe escape | To sing a song | To wait quietly | *To make holes
exercise: Mia says, «I need to drill my times tables every night.» What does drill mean here? | A tool for making holes in wood | *Repeated practice to learn something well | A fire alarm | To lose something
test: «A boy in Wellington hears the earthquake drill signal, drops under his desk, covers his head and holds on.» What does the boy do after he hears the signal? | Sings a song | *Drops under his desk | Goes home early | Runs out of the door
test: «In 2021 scientists drilling through about nine hundred metres of ice found sponges living on a rock underneath.» What does drilling mean here? | Practising a fire escape | Counting numbers out loud | Reading quietly | *Making a deep hole with a machine
exam: At the dentist, a drill cleans out a bad part of a tooth. What does drill mean in this sentence? | To sing loudly | A fire drill | *A tool or machine for making holes | Repeated practice of times tables
